libshumate (the C library)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The crate above is only a binding. The code that does the work is the C library
libshumate, which libshumate-sys resolves with pkg-config as `shumate-1.0` and
links at build time.

  https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libshumate
  Copyright 2008-2026 the libshumate contributors
  Licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later

This gem is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and that remains
true: the LGPL reaches the library it covers, not a work that links it, provided
the recipient can relink against their own copy. The gem satisfies that two
ways. The source gem compiles against whichever libshumate the installing
machine provides, so it never ships one. A precompiled platform gem must either
carry the library as a shared object the recipient can replace, or not be built
at all; it may not static-link libshumate, and nothing here configures it to.

Section 6 of the LGPL also requires that this notice say the library is used and
where to get it, which the paragraphs above do.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
gtk4-rs and gtk-rs-core
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The extension depends on the gtk4 and glib crates directly, for gtk::init, for
glib::Bytes and for glib::Value. They are the same crates libshumate itself
resolves, pinned to the same versions so that one glib type registry exists in
the process rather than two.

  https://github.com/gtk-rs/gtk4-rs
  https://github.com/gtk-rs/gtk-rs-core
  Licensed under the MIT License

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
On the GTK4 widgets
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

libshumate is mostly GtkWidget subclasses, and none of them are bound. A map
widget means nothing without a window and a main loop, and a GObject cannot be
held in a Ruby object soundly because magnus requires a wrapped type to be Send.
What is bound is the arithmetic and the parsing. See the module documentation in
ext/libshumate/src/lib.rs for the reasoning in full.
